# What the image does not need.
#
# The build stage copies the repository and compiles it; everything here is either rebuilt from
# something else or was never part of the application. Keeping it out is not tidiness — a `dist/` or
# a `node_modules/` that arrives from the host can silently disagree with the lockfile, and a `.git`
# directory in an image is a copy of the history nobody asked for.

.git
.github
node_modules
dist
test-results
playwright-report
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
backups

# Not read at runtime, and not needed to build. `e2e/` stays: `tsconfig.json` references its
# tsconfig, so removing it breaks the typecheck that `npm run build` runs first.
*.log
.opencode
.taskmaster
